            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Substitute ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "m=\\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " into point-gradient form, then divide by ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "x-x_1",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ". This requires ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "x_2\\ne x_1",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " and ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "x\\ne x_1",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ".",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p32-q9-short-qualification",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The divided form excludes ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "(x_1,y_1)",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "; the multiplied form includes it. Distinct points with ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "x_2=x_1",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " instead define the vertical line ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "x=x_1",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ".",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "For $x_2\\ne x_1$, the gradient is $m=\\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}$. Substitute into point-gradient form:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y-y_1&=m(x-x_1)\\\\y-y_1&=\\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}(x-x_1).\\end{align*}$$\n\nFor $x\\ne x_1$, divide by $x-x_1$:\n\n$$\\frac{y-y_1}{x-x_1}=\\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}.$$\n\nThe divided formula is undefined at $(x_1,y_1)$, so the forms are equivalent only on the restricted domain $x\\ne x_1$. The multiplied point-gradient form includes that given point.\n\nDistinct points with $x_2=x_1$ instead define the vertical line $x=x_1$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
